  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-boxy-atom-bnpl-email-form (npm)",
  "details": "When required, the package silently downloads and executes a second-stage binary payload from attacker-controlled infrastructure. The code in _runtime.js connects to Cloudflare Workers C2 domains (oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev) over HTTPS to fetch a platform-specific binary (linux_x64, linux_arm64, darwin, win32). If the HTTPS download fails, it falls back to DNS TXT record-based data exfiltration via c[.]tin[.]dl[.]well1[.]site (DNS tunneling). The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003crandom_hex\u003e (or C:\\Windows\\Temp\\dotnet_diag_\u003crandom_hex\u003e.exe on Windows) and spawned as a detached background process. A cache marker at /tmp/.analytics_state prevents re-downloading within ~6 hours. The package has no repository, no lifecycle scripts, and its index.js exports a benign-looking class that silently loads the downloader.",
  "affected": [
